	<string>Sidefolk reads Apple Notes and Reminders when you ask, and copies notes into its notebook. It changes nothing in them unless you approve each change.</string>
	<key>NSHumanReadableCopyright</key>
	<string>© 2026 Sidefolk</string>
	<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
	<dict>
		<!-- Sidefolk enforces its own URL policy (docs/SECURITY.md T11); users can watch plain-http sites and use local models. -->
		<key>NSAllowsArbitraryLoads</key>
		<true/>
		<key>NSAllowsLocalNetworking</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
	<key>NSSupportsAutomaticGraphicsSwitching</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Sidefolk reaches your local network only when you ask it to watch something there, or to use an AI model running on another computer.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Sidefolk listens only while you hold the talk shortcut, and understands what you say on this Mac. The recording is never kept.</string>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>On macOS 15, Sidefolk uses Apple's on-device speech recognition to understand what you say while you hold the talk shortcut.</string>
</dict>
